  A grid-item placeholder: a picture glyph. A GridTemplate requires an image
  per item, and the wire carries no bitmaps, so the host marks every item
  identically and the titles do the distinguishing. A follow-up may resolve
  known artwork ids to bundled art; until then this glyph says "image slot",
  honestly empty. Drawn here for the same reason as ic_voice: a plain white
  vector in this app's own package is the only form that survives crossing
  into the templates host process; the host tints it.
-->
